LOK: a drag in Impress outlives an unfocused window

While an action runs, DrawViewShell::MouseMove asks whether the mouse
left the window: a position outside the output area, with the window
not focused, releases the mouse and breaks the action. Under the kit
the event carries a logic position, which is almost never inside the
window's few pixels, so the answer hangs on HasFocus() alone. On
macOS, where the kit's window gains and loses focus on the system's
own time, about one drag in ten posted through setGraphicSelection
ended there: the handle was picked, the drag begun, and the move that
follows the press dropped it (Ely R17.2). A kit client has no window
edge to leave; the test is skipped under the kit.
